    ('p', 'In France, <em>haute couture</em> is a protected designation. Houses that use it officially are members of the Paris couture federation and work to strict rules: garments made to measure for private clients, an atelier with full-time craftspeople in Paris, and collections presented each season during Paris Couture Week. That is why only a small number of houses worldwide are officially "haute couture".'),
